msgid "Define a `Worker::new` function that takes an `id` number and returns a `Worker` instance that holds the `id` and a thread spawned with an empty closure."
msgstr ""

#: src/ch21-02-multithreaded.md
msgid "In `ThreadPool::new`, use the `for` loop counter to generate an `id`, create a new `Worker` with that `id`, and store the `Worker` in the vector."
msgstr ""

#: src/ch21-02-multithreaded.md
msgid "If you’re up for a challenge, try implementing these changes on your own before looking at the code in Listing 21-15."
msgstr ""

